“You” means the individual or legal entity exercising permissions under this License. If You act on behalf of an organization, You represent that You have authority to bind that organization, and “You” includes that organization.

“Software” means `@khannaoffice/unigrid`, including its source code, compiled code, documentation distributed with the package, and any modification or derivative version of the Software.

“Permitted Project” means a website or web application created, developed, operated, maintained, or delivered for end use by You, Your organization, or a client. A Permitted Project may be personal or commercial and may itself be sold, licensed, transferred, hosted, or monetized. A Reusable Software Product is excluded from the definition of a Permitted Project.

“Reusable Software Product” means software, source material, tooling, or a service whose purpose or practical effect is to make the Software, a material portion of the Software, or functionality derived from or incorporating the Software available to third parties for reuse across projects. This includes libraries, packages, frameworks, component systems, design-system products, SDKs, starter kits, reusable templates, template libraries, website builders, application builders, visual layout tools, development platforms, white-label development systems, and similar reusable development products or services.

